**POSITION**  
Supervisor, Facility Management is responsible for managing and supervising the employees under their authority, working closely with the Maintenance Centre management team. They foster a positive and engaging work environment by supporting employee development, ensuring the consistent application of collective agreements, and maintaining a safe, high-performing workplace that complies with all applicable standards and regulations.



The incumbent is responsible for planning, coordinating, and overseeing the maintenance, repair, and improvement activities of the facilities under their responsibility. They ensure the effective use of human, material, and financial resources to support operational continuity, infrastructure reliability, and compliance with schedules, budgets, and applicable standards.



The incumbent plays a key role in the delivery of operational projects and major initiatives aimed at maintaining, modernizing, and optimizing facilities. They coordinate the activities of internal teams, contractors, and suppliers, monitor project progress, and contribute to the implementation of departmental and organizational priorities. They also participate in identifying needs, defining solutions, and executing initiatives to enhance safety, efficiency, sustainability, and the overall quality of facilities and services provided to users.



Recognized for their ability to lead and engage teams, their initiative, and their results-oriented approach, the incumbent successfully addresses complex challenges and promotes a culture of continuous improvement. They leverage their operational expertise to identify opportunities for enhancement, resolve issues effectively, and contribute to excellence in service delivery and operational performance.



**RESPONSIBILITIES:**



**Supervision and Coordination of Resources and Operational Activities**

* Provide direct supervision of unionized employees assigned to facility maintenance and operations activities;
* Manage the recruitment, onboarding, training, development, and performance evaluation of employees under their responsibility;
* Ensure the consistent application of the collective agreement and maintain constructive labour relations with union representatives;
* Plan workforce requirements and coordinate the deployment of resources based on operational priorities and business needs;
* Collaborate with technical teams to facilitate the execution of facility maintenance, repair, and improvement work;
* Coordinate the activities of internal teams, contractors, and vendors involved in projects and work carried out within their area of responsibility;
* Ensure compliance with health, safety, environmental, and regulatory requirements;
* Contribute to the continuous improvement of processes and work methods to enhance operational efficiency, reliability, and safety;
* Manage employee performance and disciplinary matters, including conducting investigations, implementing corrective and disciplinary actions when required, and addressing issues related to attendance, conduct, and compliance with organizational policies and procedures, in accordance with the collective agreement and applicable policies.


**Management of Operational Projects and Major Works**

* Plan, coordinate, and oversee operational projects and major work related to facilities and infrastructure;
* Develop execution strategies and monitor project schedules to ensure timely delivery;
* Coordinate the activities of consultants, suppliers, contractors, and internal stakeholders involved in projects;
* Ensure compliance with quality, safety, and corporate standards throughout all phases of project execution;
* Ensure the seamless integration of projects into ongoing operations to minimize disruptions and maintain operational continuity;
* Support the commissioning process and facilitate the effective transfer of assets to operations and maintenance teams, ensuring a smooth transition to day-to-day management and use.


**Department Representation and Management of Interventions**

* Act as the primary point of contact for all activities and issues affecting the buildings and facilities under their responsibility;
* Coordinate the efforts of internal and external stakeholders to ensure operational continuity and minimize disruptions;
* Assess and communicate the impact of maintenance activities, projects, and operational work on building occupants and business operations;
* Monitor and ensure the quality, compliance, and completion of work performed by contractors, consultants, and service providers;
* Represent the organization's interests in matters related to the facilities and infrastructure under their responsibility;
* Facilitate effective communication between operational teams, business partners, and project stakeholders to ensure alignment on priorities and objectives;
* Support issue resolution and coordinate responses to operational incidents, emergencies, and unforeseen events affecting facility operations;
* Promote a customer-focused approach by ensuring that facility-related services meet the needs of occupants while maintaining operational and regulatory requirements.


**Data Management and Asset Management Support**

* Ensure the collection, validation, and ongoing maintenance of data related to facilities, infrastructure, and equipment;
* Maintain the accuracy, completeness, and integrity of information recorded within asset and maintenance management systems;
* Produce, monitor, and analyze key performance indicators (KPIs) to support maintenance planning, operational decision-making, and performance management;
* Identify performance gaps and recommend corrective actions to improve the reliability, efficiency, and lifecycle performance of facilities and equipment;
* Ensure the availability and quality of data required to support the organization's asset management programs and long-term capital planning initiatives;
* Support the development and maintenance of asset inventories, condition assessments, and asset lifecycle management strategies;
* Collaborate with internal stakeholders to improve data quality, reporting processes, and system utilization;
* Contribute to the optimization of asset management practices through data-driven analysis and continuous improvement initiatives;
* Prepare reports, dashboards, and operational metrics to support management decision-making and regulatory compliance requirements.


**WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR:**



* Bilingual in French and English, both spoken and written;
* Valid driver's licence;
* CROR (Canadian Rail Operating Rules) qualification is considered an asset;
* College diploma (DEC) in Electrical Engineering Technology, Building Systems Technology,

****Job Description:****
**Description D'emploi**
**Votre environnement de travail:**
Et si VOTRE aventure avec NOUS commençait ?!


Nous vous proposons de travailler chez Airbus Atlantique, nouveau champion de dimension mondiale, n°2 des aérostructures, n°1 des sièges pilotes et dans le Top 3 des fauteuils passagers Premium. Notre site Airbus Atlantique basé à Mirabel recherche son(sa) futur(e) : Directeur(trice) Programme / flux industriels afin de piloter le succès de nos programmes A220.


**Sommaire du poste:**
:


Sous la responsabilité du CEO d'Airbus Atlantique Canada, le (la) Directeur(trice) Programme / flux industriels sera en charge de la satisfaction de notre clients Airbus Canada (TCQ), de la livraison en temps, coût, qualité et performance des programmes portés par la PreFAL de Mirabel, incluant la sécurisation de la montée en cadence de l'A220.


**Responsabilités:**

* Atteindre la satisfaction de nos clients Airbus Canada en améliorant continuellement la qualité de nos produits, en livrant les workpackages de l’A220 (Pointe Avant, Aft fuselage, Bulkhead) en Temps, en Qualité et en Coût, avec un pilotage au travers de nos Quality-Gates;
* Initier, piloter le cas échéant et clôturer les activités de gestion de crise nécessaires pour assurer la fluidité des activités le long de la chaîne de valeurs des Pièces élémentaires aux sections de fuselage;
* Travailler en collaboration avec toutes les fonctions (Opérations, Qualité, Ingénierie, Achats...), assurer la synchronisation et la cascade des informations de gestion des programmes (par exemple: définition client, business planning intégré de bout en bout, configuration avion, budgets, plan de compétitivité) vers les parties prenantes;
* Piloter le macro-planning de production en fonction de la demande client et de la stratégie de montée en cadence à travers la mise en place du Master Planning Schedule (MPS);
* Gérer la relation globale avec le client grâce à des gouvernances périodiques incluant la gestion du contrat et les négociations associées (évolution de prix, gestion des options et des demandes de changements);
* Gérer la configuration des work packages incluant les demandes de changements internes, externes, leur implémentation et les impacts financiers associés;
* Gérer les risques et opportunités (R&0) pour le programme A220 (Make et Buy);
* Gérer l’enveloppe budgétaire complète des investissements OPEX et CAPEX des programmes;
* Piloter les profits et pertes (P&L) & le plan de compétitivité des WP de l’A220, conformément aux objectifs financiers cascadés, y compris les activités DtC (Design to Cost);
* Prendre la responsabilité de structurer et piloter la montée en cadence du programme A220, pour la chaîne de valeur entière (VSM) ainsi que la mise en place des gouvernances associées;
* Co-construire avec les achats la stratégie d’approvisionnement des pièces élémentaires et des workpackages incluant la gestion des réclamations RP et NRP, en accord avec la stratégie Achats de AA;
* S’assurer de la cohérence des stratégies des différentes entités et filiales d’AA en termes de worksharing, derisking, choix industriels et priorités;
* Piloter en mode MFT les projets majeurs de transformation pour s’assurer de l’atteinte des objectifs TCQP (inventaires, Transfer of Work, structure de chaîne,...).

**Missions:**

* Améliorer la satisfaction des clients (TCQ), en s’assurant de la continuité du flux de production sur l’ensemble de la chaîne de valeur, en initiant et pilotant le cas échéant les activités de gestion de crise;
* Piloter les budgets et les activités impactant les profits et pertes annuels (P&L) et les flux de trésorerie des programmes afin de réaliser des objectifs financiers (OP) et les objectifs de livraison;
* Initier et piloter le plan de compétitivité afin de tenir les objectifs de rentabilité pluriannuels;
* Garantir la robustesse de la gestion de configuration du programme, tout en pilotant l'évolution des produits au travers de la gestion des modifications (MOD);
* Assurer la mise en œuvre des modifications ou nouveaux développements potentiels, et leurs répercussions NRC / RC, sans impact sur OTD et OQD;
* Contribuer à l'élaboration des stratégies d’approvisionnement (Make to Buy, Buy to Buy), et de la stratégie industrielle;
* Mener des activités de gestion des risques, en particulier l'identification, l'évaluation, l'atténuation et le reporting exhaustifs des risques.

**Profil recherché:**

* BAC en génie aéronautique, génie industriel, administration ou discipline connexe. Maîtrise, un atout;
* Minimum de 10 ans en gestion de programmes ou de projets d'envergure dans le secteur aéronautique;
* Français parlé et écrit. Maîtrise avancée de l'anglais requis pour interagir avec les équipes internationales, fournisseurs mondiaux et partenaires d'Airbus Canada;
* Solide maîtrise du pilotage de P&L, des budgets d'investissements et du suivi des indicateurs de performance (KPI / Quality-Gates);
* Connaissance approfondie des processus de configuration avion et de gestion des modifications (MOD / NRC / RC);
* Expérience démontrée dans la gestion de la chaîne de valeur ( Value Stream Mapping ) et du Master Planning Schedule (MPS);
* Habileté avérée en négociation contractuelle, gestion de crise et leadership d'équipes pluridisciplinaires (MFT).

Ce travail nécessite une prise de conscience liée à tous les risques potentiels de conformité et à un engagement à agir avec intégrité, ces valeurs sont le fondement du succès, de la réputation et de la croissance durable de l'entreprise.


